[job_20261010_4ca1c594] resolve.decision: Annual income Rs 21,001, just above the limit: verifier_wrong. The rulebook income condition follows the document. Appendix-1 row 3 (page 11) sets the limit at 'रुपये २१,०००/- पर्यंत' (up to Rs 21,000), and page 8 clause 6 sets Rs 21,000 for all non-disabled beneficiaries. The rule `annual_family_income <= 21000 or (disabled and annual_family_income <= 50000)` is therefore correct. Rs 21,001 is above the limit, so a non-disabled person fails it. The mismatch comes from the test person, which is incomplete. It leaves out `disabled`, so the rule cannot tell whether the Rs 50,000 disabled limit applies. It also leaves out `years_in_maharashtra`, which the 15-year residency rule needs. Because of the missing fields the engine returned an eligible result with no unmet conditions. The verifier's expected outcome (not eligible) is what the document says, but the test is not a valid check of the rulebook. It should be rebuilt with `disabled: false` and `years_in_maharashtra >= 15`. The rulebook does not need to change.
